der-color\" data-source=\"Version Added\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Version Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Date Added</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">?</div>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"Status\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Status</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">Obtainable</div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\n\t</section>\n\n\n\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span></h2>\n<p>The <b>Dogwood</b> tree is one of the various trees that can be found in <a href=\"/wiki/Flowering_Meadows\" title=\"Flowering Meadows\">Flowering Meadows</a>. It looks similar to the <a href=\"/wiki/Sakura\" title=\"Sakura\">Sakura</a> tree but it's leaves slightly brighter, and trunk more brown-grayish.  Also on it's leaves you can find <a href=\"/wiki/Dogwood_blossom\" title=\"Dogwood blossom\">Dogwood blossom</a>.\n</p><p>Like every other material in-game, it can be used to complete schematics.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Textures\">Textures</span></h2><p>\nThe various textures of the <b>Dogwood</b> in its raw/log, sanded, and planked states.</p><div id=\"gallery-1\" hash=\"9f78881edab3d290d143462d0cbaa0a9\" data-seq-no=\"1\" class=\"wikia-gallery wikia-gallery-caption-below wikia-gallery-position-left wikia-gallery-spacing-medium wikia-gallery-border-small wikia-gallery-captions-left wikia-gallery-caption-size-medium\"><div class=\"wikia-gallery-caption\"></div><div class=\"wikia-gallery-item\" style=\"width:102px; \"><div class=\"thumb\" style=\"height:102px;\"><div class=\"gallery-image-wrapper accent\" id=\"DogwoodLogT-png\" style=\"position: relative; height:100px; width:99px